    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "AMOVE is delighted to bring this charming, cleverly extended, B rated home to the market.  Exceptionally well located just outside Nurney village, and just 9 minutes’ drive from Kildare town (7.5km) & 7km from junction 13 onto the M7 at Kildare Village.  This smart home, displays an on trend interior that was completely remodelled in 2018/19.   \r\n\r\nAccommodation comprises:  Hall, Lounge, Kitchen / Breakfast room, 3 bedrooms, with the master being ensuite and a house bathroom.\r\n\r\nThis tasteful, exceptionally pretty property offers discerning buyers, a large site overlooking farmland to  its large garden, a cobble locked wrap around patio, ideal for outdoor dining / lounging, ample off street parking and a block built 32sqm workshop that could be converted if required.  This property also has a large attic that can be converted to extra living space if required.  \r\n\r\nViewing comes highly recommended"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall: Laminate floor, radiator cover, stira attic hatch, ceiling downlighters, \r\n\r\nLounge: Laminate floor, polished pine mantlepiece, with granite hearth to open fire with cast iron inset surround, feature wallpaper wall, window overlooking front garden & drive \r\n\r\nKitchen / dining room:  contemporary kitchen with high & low kitchen cabinets integrated double Oven, 4 ring Logik - induction electric hob with extractor hood over, integrated dishwasher, fridge freezer, tiled over worktops large inset sssu with, window overlooking rear garden, patio doors to rear, laminte floor and ample room for a dining table & reading area.\r\n\r\nUtility Room:  off hallway plumbed for washing machine & dryer, good storage space\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (front) Master: large double room, carpeted floors,  window overlooking gardens, floor to ceiling fitted wardrobes door to\r\n\r\nEn-Suite:  fully tiled floors & part tiled walls, w.c, vanity whb. Fully enclosed large step in shower with Triton electric shower, chrome heated towel rail & window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (rear):  double room, laminate floors, window overlooking rear garden\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (rear): single room, laminate floors, window overlooking rear garden \r\n\r\nHouse Bathroom: fully tiled floor and part tiled walls, w.c., w.h.b with dark wood cabinet under, with light over, enclosed bath, with telephone shower hose, chrome heated towel rail & window to side\r\n\r\nOUTSIDE\r\nTo the front / side:\r\nTo the front the property is a walled and enclosed garden with a large driveway, cobblelocked pathway around the house.  Vehicular access to side & rear of the house if required.  \r\n\r\nTo the rear: \r\nExceptionally large rear garden measures 20m (65’6”ft) long x 14m (45’9”ft) wide with a wonderfully private outlook that enjoys westerly sunshine to its rear patio.  Large cobblelocked patio and pathway around house, outside tap and lighting OFCH boiler.  Fully enclosed boundary wall and fence with an open outlook over green fields\r\n\r\nDetached workshop – 8.8m x 3.66m pitched roof block built with concrete floor & full power, double glazed window & door."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Beautifully appointed & presented 3 bed semi bungalow with bright & airy accommodation – 104sqm (1,119sq.ft) with a detached workshop & vehicular side access if required.\r\nRefurbished & extended in 2018/19 – Double Glazed throughout, walls slabbed with insulation, new concrete floors installed, energy efficient OFCH boiler with back boiler to stove, mains services – B BER\r\nExceptionally large rear garden measures 20m (65’6”ft) long x 14m (45’9”ft) wide with a wonderfully private outlook that enjoys westerly sunshine to its rear patio.\r\nAmple driveway with a cobble lock pathway and rear patio.\r\nWithin minutes of a Nurney primary school, local shops & a village pub.\r\n7km from Kildare village, 4.3km from Kildangan and 8.5km from Monasterevin and just 50km from Newlands Cross in Dublin (train stations in Kildare & Monasterevin)\r\nBus stop outside house ‘Local link’ stopping in Kildare & Newbridge"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: B3"
      }
